This repository is a Python wrapper and a local/LAN web panel. Its own
source is this project, also under LGPL-3.0-or-later. Release wheels and
zips additionally ship pre-built, self-contained MuConvert binaries. The
Corresponding Source for one of those binaries is the upstream MuConvert
tree at the commit that produced it.

v0.6.0b1 does not pin an upstream tag or commit. `python3 -m muconvert
--build` clones the default branch of https://github.com/MuNET-OSS/MuConvert
(or reuses an existing checkout under vendor/MuConvert-src or
~/.cache/muconvert/MuConvert-src) and runs `dotnet publish`. A later build
fetches tags and keeps that checkout; it does not switch to a fixed tag.

Anyone who ships a pre-built binary should record and publish, alongside
that wheel or zip:

  - the upstream commit SHA (and tag, if any), for example
    `git -C vendor/MuConvert-src rev-parse HEAD`
  - the version string printed by `MuConvert --version` / `muconvert --version`

Recipients can rebuild from that same commit with `python3 -m muconvert
--build`, or by cloning the commit and following the Build section of
README.md.

